@startuml distribution
' SPEC: _spec/distribution.puml
' purpose: Distribution architecture — UI + CoachService + shell across mediums; Android embedded server + P2P transport decision.
' constraint: ONE coach port; VITE_TARGET picks wiring at compile time; behaviour-defining prompt logic shared via @chess-coach/engine-core.
!include themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

title Chess Coach · Distribution\nUI + CoachService + shell · matrix · Android · transport

package "The one idea — UI + CoachService + shell" as ONE {

  class "SolidJS UI (apps/ui)" as UI <<app>> {
    VITE_TARGET: web-no-llm · web-full · desktop
  }

  interface "CoachService port\nservices/api.ts" as CSP

  class "HttpCoachService" as HTTP <<app>> {
    desktop / Docker line
  }

  class "WebWorkerCoachService" as WW <<app>> {
    web / Android line
  }

  class "Bun server (apps/server)" as BUN <<app>> {
    in-process Orchestrator (no daemon)
  }

  class "native Stockfish + lc0 (Maia)" as NATIVE <<app>> {
    Bun.spawn subprocesses
  }

  class "Ollama / LLM" as OLLAMA <<cloud>> {
    commentary · advice · explain
  }

  class "browser workers" as WORKERS <<async>> {
    orchestrator.worker · maia.worker
  }

  class "Stockfish WASM + lc0.wasm" as WASM <<async>> {
    SAB budget shared with UI hints
  }

  class "WebLLM (WebGPU)" as WEBLLM <<async>> {
    chess-gemma-commentary on-device
  }

  note as N_CORE
    Behavior-defining prompt / classification / commentary logic is **one shared
    implementation** (""@chess-coach/engine-core"") pinned by
    ""apps/server/behavior.md""; parity map in
    ""packages/engine-core/ui-engine-parity.md"".
  end note

  N_CORE .. UI
}

package "Mediums" as MED {

  class "Web · Cloudflare\nPages / Workers" as WEB <<host>> {
    exists — /chess path
  }

  class "Docker desktop\nroot Dockerfile" as DOCKER <<host>> {
    exists — UI + native engines + Bun
  }

  class "Desktop app\nTauri / bun build --compile" as DESK <<host>> {
    proposed
  }

  class "Android\nWebView → embedded Go server" as AND <<host>> {
    scaffolded (apps/android)
  }

  note as N_STATUS
    **Status:**
    * Web (Cloudflare) — **exists**
    * Docker desktop — **exists**
    * Desktop app — **proposed**
    * Android — **scaffolded** (WIP)

    Medium = **UI + a chosen CoachService + a shell** — nothing new in engine
    code to add a shell, only packaging.
  end note
}

package "Android — embedded thin server + WASM WebView + P2P" as AN {

  class "Go server (net/http + tsnet)\nforeground service" as GO <<host>> {
    serves web-full over loopback 127.0.0.1
    COOP: same-origin · COEP: require-corp
    owns tailnet WSS / WebRTC signaling
    persists game/session state (survives churn)
    IS NOT the desktop coach endpoints
  }

  class "WebView (web-full build)" as WV <<app>> {
    WebWorkerCoachService client-side
  }

  class "Tailscale tailnet" as TS <<cloud>> {
    WireGuard mesh + DERP relays
  }

  class "Model A infra\nCloudflare DO signaling + STUN/TURN" as A_INFRA <<cloud>> {
    only when Model A chosen
  }

  note as N_ANDROID
    **Why a server in the app (2026-06-24 decisions):**
    * Secure context for free (""localhost"" is potentially trustworthy) — no TLS
      for RTCPeerConnection / SharedArrayBuffer.
    * Header control — COOP/COEP ⇒ cross-origin isolation ⇒ threaded WASM.
    * Lifecycle — peer/signaling socket owned by a foreground service survives
      rotation/backgrounding (a WebView-owned peer dies).
    * State survives churn — FEN/history + P2P session persisted for resume.

    The embedded server is a **thin host**: coach runs client-side, so /move,
    /advice, /explain are NOT used on-device.
  end note

  N_ANDROID .. GO
}

note as N_TRANSPORT
  **Transport — audience decides (2026-06-24).**
  * **Model A — WebRTC + hosted signaling + STUN/TURN:** open / public peers
    (strangers). Signaling = Cloudflare DO/Worker WebSocket; STUN = public;
    TURN = coturn (cellular symmetric NAT). Protocol: SDP/ICE/data-channel.
  * **Model B — Tailscale mesh:** known group (friends / own devices),
    **recommended when it fits**. WireGuard = direct path, DERP = relay fallback —
    no STUN/TURN/self-hosted signaling. A plain WSS between the two in-app
    servers replaces WebRTC. Cost: both peers must join the same tailnet.

  **P2P engine delta:** ""executeTurn"" / Maia move-gen is bypassed (opponent move
  arrives via data channel); hints + commentary stay local per device. A P2P game
  is two independent local coaches over a shared move stream.
end note

UI ARROW_MAIN CSP : selects
CSP ARROW_OPTIONAL HTTP : desktop / Docker
CSP ARROW_OPTIONAL WW : web / Android
HTTP ARROW_MAIN BUN : HTTP REST
BUN ARROW_MAIN NATIVE : UCI (Bun.spawn)
BUN ARROW_CLOUD OLLAMA : OpenAI-compatible HTTP
WW ARROW_QUEUE WORKERS : postMessage
WORKERS ARROW_MAIN WASM : UCI
WORKERS ARROW_MAIN WEBLLM : prompt/stream
UI ARROW_MAIN WEB : deployed to
BUN ARROW_MAIN DOCKER : packaged in
UI ARROW_OPTIONAL DESK : wraps in (proposed)
UI ARROW_OPTIONAL AND : serves in (scaffolded)
GO ARROW_MAIN WV : serves web-full (loopback)
WV ARROW_OPTIONAL GO : injects ChessNative bridge
GO ARROW_CLOUD TS : tailnet peer link
TS ARROW_OPTIONAL A_INFRA : Model A only

note bottom of AN
  **Related:** ""apps/android/webrtc-p2p.puml"" (peer/signaling details) ·
  ""architecture.puml"" (deployment topology) ·
  ""apps/server/behavior.md"" (backend contract).
end note

note bottom
  **Open decisions / risks:**
  * Transport model — decide audience first: Model A (strangers) vs Model B (Tailscale).
  * tsnet on Android via gomobile; AAR size (limit ABIs to arm64); foreground-service lifecycle.
  * Model A peer — native libwebrtc in service (stable) vs JS RTCPeerConnection (dies on WebView recreation).
  * Reconnect/resume semantics — whose state is authoritative; move-number reconciliation.
  * Matchmaking (rooms/links/lobby) — out of scope here.
end note

@enduml
